{"id":"n5-091","title":"だれか〜","romaji":"dareka〜","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Indicates 'someone' or something done or possessed by 'someone'.","longExplanation":"The grammar point だれか〜 is used to suggest that something is done by, possessed by, or related to 'someone', usually when the actual person is unidentified or not important. It can be used with verbs, adjectives, or nouns.","formation":"だれか + Verb, だれか + Adjective, だれか + Noun","examples":[{"jp":"だれかがドアをノックしました。","romaji":"Dareka ga doa wo nokku shimashita.","en":"Someone knocked on the door.","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ドア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ノック","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"だれかが私の傘を盗みました。","romaji":"Dareka ga watashi no kasa wo nusumimashita.","en":"Someone stole my umbrella.","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"私","vocabId":"1311110","reading":"わたし"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"傘","vocabId":"1301940","reading":"かさ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"盗み","vocabId":"1448400","reading":"ぬすみ","baseForm":"盗む"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"だれか助けてください。","romaji":"Dareka tasukete kudasai.","en":"Someone, please help.","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"助け","vocabId":"1344390","reading":"たすけ","baseForm":"助ける"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":